Notebook[{
Cell["Graphical calculus \:00a72.7.3\:20132.7.4 and \:00a73.1\:20133.2.3: proj_k, braidings, Reidemeister diagrams", "Title"],
Cell["Turaev & Virelizier, Monoidal Categories and Topological Field Theory, pp. 50\:201358 \:00b7 sections 50\:201356 \:00b7 continues the notebooks for \:00a72.1\:20132.7", "Subtitle"],
Cell["By Dara O Shayda and Noor Hoshino (\:661f\:91ce\:30cc\:30fc\:30eb)", "Text"],
Cell["49. Setup", "Section"],
Cell["The first cell loads the engine from this folder (Desktop/Research/Monoidal Graphical Calculus). The code of this notebook is also saved on its own as braided-2.7-3.2.wl, which the GraphicalCalculusKernel loads.", "Text"],
Cell["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n(* the engine: sections 0\:201319, 20\:201327, 30\:201335 and 40\:201347, all in this folder *)\ndir = FileNameJoin[{$HomeDirectory, \"Desktop\", \"Research\", \"Monoidal Graphical Calculus\"}];\nWith[{cells = Cases[Get[FileNameJoin[{dir, \"graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb\"}]], Cell[c_, \"Input\" | \"Code\", ___] :> c, Infinity]},\n Scan[Quiet@Check[TimeConstrained[ToExpression[#, StandardForm]; Null, 120], Null] &, cells];\n Print[\"Loaded \", Length[cells], \" code cells from graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb\"]];\ndir = FileNameJoin[{$HomeDirectory, \"Desktop\", \"Research\", \"Monoidal Graphical Calculus\"}];\nQuiet[Get[FileNameJoin[{dir, #}]]] & /@ {\"pivotal-2.1.3.wl\", \"penrose-2.2.wl\", \"pivotal-2.3-2.7.wl\"};\nPrint[\"Loaded pivotal-2.1.3.wl, penrose-2.2.wl and pivotal-2.3-2.7.wl\"];", "Input"],
Cell["50. \:00a72.7.3 Sphericity of proj_k: Lemma 2.10", "Section"],
Cell["A projective module X of finite type sits in a free module Y = X \:2295 R: j : X \:2192 Y is the inclusion and p : Y \:2192 X the projection, so p j = id_X while j p is only an idempotent of Y.\n   Lemma 2.10 says tr_l(f) is the Hattori\:2013Stallings trace Tr(j f p). The proof is the graphical identity tr_l(j f p) = tr_l(f p j) = tr_l(f): trace symmetry, then p j = id_X.\n   \"retract\" is that one-sided cancellation: a box p directly above a box j on the same line cancels when the pair {p, j} is declared in retracts.", "Text"],
Cell["retracts = {{\"p\", \"j\"}};                         (* p \:2218 j = id *)\ncancelRetract[{a_, B[j_, {x_}, {y_}]}, {a_, B[p_, {y_}, {x_}]}] /; MemberQ[retracts, {p, j}] := {};\ncancelRetract[__] := $Failed;", "Input"],
Cell["51. \:00a73.1.1 Braidings: the boxes \:03c4_X,Y and \:03c4\:207b\:00b9_Y,X, and the rules (3.1)\:2013(3.3)", "Section"],
Cell["\:03c4_X,Y : X \:2297 Y \:2192 Y \:2297 X is drawn as a crossing in which the strand coming from X passes over (Figure 3.1). The other crossing is \:03c4\:207b\:00b9_Y,X : X \:2297 Y \:2192 Y \:2297 X, the inverse of \:03c4_Y,X.\n   The subscript is the string \"X,Y\"; X and Y may be tensor products such as \"X\:2297Y\".\n   (3.1) \:03c4_X,Y\:2297Z = (id_Y \:2297 \:03c4_X,Z)(\:03c4_X,Y \:2297 id_Z) and (3.2) \:03c4_X\:2297Y,Z = (\:03c4_X,Z \:2297 id_Y)(id_X \:2297 \:03c4_Y,Z) split a crossing of tensor products into crossings of single lines; (3.3) \:03c4_X,\|01d7d9 = \:03c4_\|01d7d9,X = id_X.", "Text"],
Cell["tauSub[x_String, y_String] := x <> \",\" <> y;\ntau[x_, y_] := Subscript[\"\\[Tau]\", tauSub[x, y]];\ntauInv[y_, x_] := Subscript[Superscript[\"\\[Tau]\", \"-1\"], tauSub[y, x]];\npartsU[x_String] := DeleteCases[partsOf[x], unit | \"\\[DoubleStruckOne]\" | \"I\" | \"1\"];\ntauB[x_, y_] := B[tau[x, y], Join[partsU[x], partsU[y]], Join[partsU[y], partsU[x]]];        (* X \:2297 Y \:2192 Y \:2297 X *)\ntauInvB[y_, x_] := B[tauInv[y, x], Join[partsU[x], partsU[y]], Join[partsU[y], partsU[x]]];  (* X \:2297 Y \:2192 Y \:2297 X, the inverse of \:03c4_Y,X *)\ntauQ[s_] := MatchQ[s, Subscript[\"\\[Tau]\" | Superscript[\"\\[Tau]\", \"-1\"], _String]];\ntauArgs[Subscript[_, s_String]] := StringSplit[s, \",\", 2];\ntauPos[s_] := MatchQ[s, Subscript[\"\\[Tau]\", _]];\n\nbraidSplit[{a_, B[s_?tauQ, i_, o_]}] := Module[{x, y, px, py},\n   {x, y} = tauArgs[s]; px = partsU[x]; py = partsU[y];\n   Which[\n    px === {} || py === {}, {},                                                             (* (3.3) *)\n    tauPos[s] && Length[py] > 1, {{a, tauB[x, First[py]]}, {a + 1, tauB[x, joinParts[Rest[py]]]}},          (* (3.1) *)\n    tauPos[s] && Length[px] > 1, {{a + 1, tauB[joinParts[Rest[px]], y]}, {a, tauB[First[px], y]}},          (* (3.2) *)\n    ! tauPos[s] && Length[py] > 1, {{a + 1, tauInvB[x, joinParts[Rest[py]]]}, {a, tauInvB[x, First[py]]}},   (* inverse of (3.1) *)\n    ! tauPos[s] && Length[px] > 1, {{a, tauInvB[First[px], y]}, {a + 1, tauInvB[joinParts[Rest[px]], y]}},   (* inverse of (3.2) *)\n    True, $Failed]];\nbraidSplit[_] := $Failed;", "Input"],
Cell["52. \:00a73.2.2 The Reidemeister moves R2\:2013R5 as rules", "Section"],
Cell["R2: a crossing and the inverse crossing on the same two lines cancel.\n   R4, R5: a box slides through a crossing (naturality of \:03c4): a one-line box just above a crossing moves below it, onto the same strand.\n   R3: the Yang\:2013Baxter equation (Exercise 3.1.12), (\:03c4_Y,Z \:2297 id_X)(id_Y \:2297 \:03c4_X,Z)(\:03c4_X,Y \:2297 id_Z) = (id_Z \:2297 \:03c4_X,Y)(\:03c4_X,Z \:2297 id_Y)(id_X \:2297 \:03c4_Y,Z), used from left to right on three consecutive crossings of the same kind.", "Text"],
Cell["crossingB[pos_, {l_String, r_String}] := If[pos, tauB[l, r], tauInvB[r, l]];      (* the crossing on the lines l, r *)\ninvTau[Subscript[\"\\[Tau]\", s_String]] := Subscript[Superscript[\"\\[Tau]\", \"-1\"], s];\ninvTau[Subscript[Superscript[\"\\[Tau]\", \"-1\"], s_String]] := Subscript[\"\\[Tau]\", s];\ncancelCross[{a_, B[s1_?tauQ, {l_, r_}, {r_, l_}]}, {a_, B[s2_?tauQ, {r_, l_}, {l_, r_}]}] /; s2 === invTau[s1] := {};\ncancelCross[__] := $Failed;\nplainBoxQ[s_] := StringQ[s];\nnaturalTau[{a_, B[s_?tauQ, {l_, r_}, {r_, l_}]}, {a_, B[g_?plainBoxQ, {r_}, {r2_}]}] :=\n  {{a + 1, B[g, {r}, {r2}]}, {a, crossingB[tauPos[s], {l, r2}]}};\nnaturalTau[{a_, B[s_?tauQ, {l_, r_}, {r_, l_}]}, {b_, B[g_?plainBoxQ, {l_}, {l2_}]}] /; b == a + 1 :=\n  {{a, B[g, {l}, {l2}]}, {a, crossingB[tauPos[s], {l2, r}]}};\nnaturalTau[__] := $Failed;\nyangBaxter[LD[src_, ls_]] := Module[{rs = rows[LD[src, ls]]},\n   Catch[Do[With[{c1 = ls[[k]], c2 = ls[[k + 1]], c3 = ls[[k + 2]]},\n      If[tauQ[sym[c1[[2]]]] && tauQ[sym[c2[[2]]]] && tauQ[sym[c3[[2]]]] &&\n        Length[ins[c1[[2]]]] == Length[ins[c2[[2]]]] == Length[ins[c3[[2]]]] == 2 &&\n        c2[[1]] == c1[[1]] + 1 && c3[[1]] == c1[[1]] &&\n        Equal @@ (tauPos /@ (sym /@ {c1[[2]], c2[[2]], c3[[2]]})),\n       With[{a = c1[[1]], e = tauPos[sym[c1[[2]]]], row = rs[[k]]},\n        Module[{x = row[[a + 1]], y = row[[a + 2]], z = row[[a + 3]]},\n         Throw[LD[src, Join[Take[ls, k - 1],\n            {{a + 1, crossingB[e, {y, z}]}, {a, crossingB[e, {x, z}]}, {a + 1, crossingB[e, {x, y}]}}, Drop[ls, k + 2]]]]]]]],\n     {k, Length[ls] - 2}]; $Failed]];\n\n(* \:00a73.1.2 symmetries and Remark 3.2.3: if \:03c4 is symmetric, \:03c4\:207b\:00b9_Y,X = \:03c4_X,Y, so over- and under-passes do not matter *)\nsymmetricTau[{a_, B[s_, i_, o_]}] /; tauQ[s] && ! tauPos[s] := With[{yx = tauArgs[s]}, {{a, B[tau[yx[[2]], yx[[1]]], i, o]}}];\nsymmetricTau[_] := $Failed;\n\nbraidRules = <|\n   \"braiding on \\[CircleTimes] (3.1)\\[Dash](3.3)\" -> {1, braidSplit},\n   \"retract (\\[Section]2.7.3)\" -> {2, cancelRetract},\n   \"R2 (\\[Section]3.2.2)\" -> {2, cancelCross},\n   \"R4, R5: naturality of \\[Tau]\" -> {2, naturalTau},\n   \"R3: Yang\\[Dash]Baxter\" -> {\"ld\", yangBaxter}|>;\ncancelSym[{a_, B[Subscript[\"\\[Tau]\", s1_String], {l_, r_}, {r_, l_}]}, {a_, B[Subscript[\"\\[Tau]\", s2_String], {r_, l_}, {l_, r_}]}] := {};\ncancelSym[__] := $Failed;\nsymRules = <|\"symmetry (\\[Section]3.1.2)\" -> {1, symmetricTau}, \"\\[Tau]_Y,X \\[Tau]_X,Y = id (\\[Section]3.1.2)\" -> {2, cancelSym}|>;\n\nrulesB = Join[rules, braidRules];          (* braided monoidal, duals written \:2228X *)\nrulesDB = Join[rulesD, braidRules];        (* braided pivotal *)\nrulesSB = Join[rulesS, braidRules];        (* braided spherical *)\nwithSymmetry[rs_Association] := Join[rs, symRules];", "Input"],
Cell["53. A matrix model: graded vector spaces with a bicharacter (Examples 3.1.4\:20133.1.6)", "Section"],
Cell["Each colour X is k^n with a grade g(X) in \:2124; g(X* ) = \:2212g(X), grades add over \:2297. The braiding is c(g, h) times the flip, with c(g, h) = q^(g h) (Example 3.1.6 with \:03b1 = 1).\n   q = \:22121 and grades mod 2 give super vector spaces (Example 3.1.5); q = 1 gives the flip of Example 3.1.4. The braiding is symmetric exactly when c(h, g) c(g, h) = 1.\n   Duality is the usual pairing (weights 1), so the category is spherical. Boxes must keep the grade.", "Text"],
Cell["gradeOf[c_String, gr_] := Which[\n   StringStartsQ[c, \"(\"], -gradeOf[StringTake[c, {2, -3}], gr],\n   StringContainsQ[c, \"\\[CircleTimes]\"], Total[gradeOf[#, gr] & /@ StringSplit[c, \"\\[CircleTimes]\"]],\n   starQ[c], -gradeOf[unstar[c], gr], True, gr[c]];\nflipM[m_, n_] := Normal[SparseArray[Flatten[Table[{(j - 1) m + i, (i - 1) n + j} -> 1, {i, m}, {j, n}], 1], {m n, m n}]];\nmatG[ld_LD, n_, gr_, q_, mats_] := Module[{rs = rows[ld], m, dimC, box},\n   dimC[cs_List] := Times @@ (nOf[#, n] & /@ cs);\n   box[b_B] := With[{s = sym[b]},\n     Which[\n      tauQ[s] && Length[ins[b]] == 2,\n       With[{l = ins[b][[1]], r = ins[b][[2]]},\n        If[tauPos[s], q^(gradeOf[l, gr] gradeOf[r, gr]), q^(-gradeOf[l, gr] gradeOf[r, gr])] flipM[nOf[l, n], nOf[r, n]]],\n      tauQ[s], matG[LD[ins[b], braidSplit[{0, b}]], n, gr, q, mats],\n      True, matBox[b, n, (1 &), mats]]];\n   m = IdentityMatrix[dimC[First[rs]]];\n   Do[With[{a = ld[[2, k, 1]], b = ld[[2, k, 2]], row = rs[[k]]},\n     m = KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[dimC[Take[row, a]]], box[b], IdentityMatrix[dimC[Drop[row, a + Length[ins[b]]]]]] . m], {k, Length[ld[[2]]]}];\n   m];", "Input"],
Cell["54. The constructions of pp. 50\:201358, as layered diagrams", "Section"],
Cell["SeedRandom[3021];\nnG = (2 &);  grG = <|\"X\" -> 1, \"Y\" -> 2, \"Z\" -> 1, \"U\" -> 1|>;  qG = 3;     (* braided, not symmetric *)\ngrS = <|\"X\" -> 1, \"Y\" -> 0, \"Z\" -> 1, \"U\" -> 1|>;                          (* super vector spaces with q = \:22121 *)\nmatsG = <|\"f\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}], \"g\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}], \"k\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}],\n    \"p\" -> {{1, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}}, \"j\" -> {{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {0, 0}}|>;\nmG[ld_, q_: qG, gr_: grG] := matG[ld, nG, gr, q, matsG];\ninG[{l__}, q_: qG, gr_: grG] := Equal @@ (mG[#, q, gr] & /@ {l});\n\n(* \:00a72.7.3: Lemma 2.10 with X = k\:00b2 inside Y = k\:00b3 *)\nnHS = <|\"X\" -> 2, \"Y\" -> 3|>;\nfXX = boxL[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}];  jB = boxL[\"j\", {\"X\"}, {\"Y\"}];  pB3 = boxL[\"p\", {\"Y\"}, {\"X\"}];\nlem210 = <|\"tr_l(j f p) = tr_l(f)\" -> {trL[stackL[pB3, fXX, jB]], trL[fXX]}|>;\nhsTrace := With[{m = matsG}, {Tr[m[\"j\"] . m[\"f\"] . m[\"p\"]], First[First[matW[trL[fXX], (nHS[#] &), (1 &), matsG]]]}];\n\n(* \:00a73.1.1 *)\nbr = <|\n   \"(3.1) \\[Tau]_X,Y\\[CircleTimes]Z = (id_Y \\[CircleTimes] \\[Tau]_X,Z)(\\[Tau]_X,Y \\[CircleTimes] id_Z)\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\\[CircleTimes]Z\"]}}],\n      LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}, {1, tauB[\"X\", \"Z\"]}}]},\n   \"(3.2) \\[Tau]_X\\[CircleTimes]Y,Z = (\\[Tau]_X,Z \\[CircleTimes] id_Y)(id_X \\[CircleTimes] \\[Tau]_Y,Z)\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\", \"Z\"]}}],\n      LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{1, tauB[\"Y\", \"Z\"]}, {0, tauB[\"X\", \"Z\"]}}]},\n   \"naturality: \\[Tau]_X',Y (f \\[CircleTimes] g) = (g \\[CircleTimes] f) \\[Tau]_X,Y\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, B[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]}, {1, B[\"g\", {\"Y\"}, {\"Y\"}]}, {0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}}],\n      LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}, {0, B[\"g\", {\"Y\"}, {\"Y\"}]}, {1, B[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]}}]},\n   \"inverse of (3.1)\" -> {LD[{\"Y\", \"Z\", \"X\"}, {{0, tauInvB[\"X\", \"Y\\[CircleTimes]Z\"]}}], LD[{\"Y\", \"Z\", \"X\"}, {{1, tauInvB[\"X\", \"Z\"]}, {0, tauInvB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}}]},\n   \"Exercise 3.1.12: Yang\\[Dash]Baxter\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}, {1, tauB[\"X\", \"Z\"]}, {0, tauB[\"Y\", \"Z\"]}}],\n      LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{1, tauB[\"Y\", \"Z\"]}, {0, tauB[\"X\", \"Z\"]}, {1, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}}]},\n   \"Exercise 3.1.12: naturality for the box \\[Tau]_Y,Z gives Yang\\[Dash]Baxter\" -> {\n      LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{1, tauB[\"Y\", \"Z\"]}, {0, tauB[\"X\", \"Z\\[CircleTimes]Y\"]}}], LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\\[CircleTimes]Z\"]}, {0, tauB[\"Y\", \"Z\"]}}]}|>;\n(* Reidemeister moves R2\:2013R5 (Figure 3.2) *)\nrm = <|\n   \"R2: \\[Tau]\\:207b\\:00b9_X,Y \\[Tau]_X,Y = id\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}, {0, tauInvB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}}], idL[{\"X\", \"Y\"}]},\n   \"R2: \\[Tau]_X,Y \\[Tau]\\:207b\\:00b9_X,Y = id\" -> {LD[{\"Y\", \"X\"}, {{0, tauInvB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}, {0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}}], idL[{\"Y\", \"X\"}]},\n   \"R3 with inverse crossings\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{0, tauInvB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}, {1, tauInvB[\"Z\", \"X\"]}, {0, tauInvB[\"Z\", \"Y\"]}}],\n      LD[{\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}, {{1, tauInvB[\"Z\", \"Y\"]}, {0, tauInvB[\"Z\", \"X\"]}, {1, tauInvB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}}]},\n   \"R4: a strand over a box\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}, {1, B[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]}}], LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, B[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]}, {0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}}]},\n   \"R5: a strand under a box\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauInvB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}, {1, B[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]}}], LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, B[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]}, {0, tauInvB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}}]},\n   \"Lemma 3.1, an upward strand: a crossing of X* passes a box\" -> {LD[{\"X*\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X*\", \"Y\"]}, {0, B[\"g\", {\"Y\"}, {\"Y\"}]}}],\n      LD[{\"X*\", \"Y\"}, {{1, B[\"g\", {\"Y\"}, {\"Y\"}]}, {0, tauB[\"X*\", \"Y\"]}}]}|>;\n(* \:00a73.1.2 symmetries, Remark 3.2.3 *)\nsy = <|\"\\[Tau]_Y,X \\[Tau]_X,Y = id\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}, {0, tauB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}}], idL[{\"X\", \"Y\"}]},\n    \"Remark 3.2.3: over and under passes agree\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauInvB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}}], LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}}]}|>;\n(* \:00a73.1.7 the mirror braiding \:03c4\:0304_X,Y = \:03c4\:207b\:00b9_Y,X also satisfies (3.1), (3.2) and Yang\:2013Baxter *)\nmirror[ld_LD] := ld /. {B[Subscript[\"\\[Tau]\", s_String], i_, o_] :> With[{xy = StringSplit[s, \",\", 2]}, B[tauInv[xy[[2]], xy[[1]]], i, o]],\n     B[Subscript[Superscript[\"\\[Tau]\", \"-1\"], s_String], i_, o_] :> With[{yx = StringSplit[s, \",\", 2]}, B[tau[yx[[2]], yx[[1]]], i, o]]};", "Input"],
Cell["55. Checking: rules and the graded model", "Section"],
Cell["byRulesB[{l__}, rs_: rulesDB] := SameQ @@ (simplifyLD[#, rs] & /@ {l});\nstepsKeepG[ld_, rs_: rulesDB, q_: qG, gr_: grG] := Equal @@ (mG[#[[2]], q, gr] & /@ simplifyTrace[ld, rs]);", "Input"],
Cell["55a. Walkthrough", "Section"],
Cell["\:00a72.7.3 Lemma 2.10", "Subsection"],
Cell["tr_l(j f p) reduces to tr_l(f): the loop is turned so that it starts at f, and p j = id_X cancels. The Hattori\:2013Stallings trace Tr(j f p) and tr_l(f) agree as numbers:", "Text"],
Cell["Column[{showTraceP[simplifyTrace[lem210[[1, 1]], rulesDB]], hsTrace}]", "Input"],
Cell["\:00a73.1.1 braidings", "Subsection"],
Cell["(3.1) splits a crossing of X over Y \:2297 Z into two crossings:", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[br[[1, 1]], rulesDB]]", "Input"],
Cell["Exercise 3.1.12: naturality of \:03c4 for the box \:03c4_Y,Z, written with the crossings of tensor products, becomes the Yang\:2013Baxter equation after (3.1) and (3.2):", "Text"],
Cell["Column[{showTraceP[simplifyTrace[br[[6, 1]], rulesDB]], showTraceP[simplifyTrace[br[[6, 2]], rulesDB]]}, Spacings -> 2]", "Input"],
Cell["\:00a73.2.2 Reidemeister moves", "Subsection"],
Cell["R4: a box slides under a strand that passes over it; R2: a crossing and its inverse cancel.", "Text"],
Cell["Column[{showTraceP[simplifyTrace[rm[[4, 1]], rulesDB]], showTraceP[simplifyTrace[rm[[1, 1]], rulesDB]]}, Spacings -> 2]", "Input"],
Cell["\:00a73.1.2 symmetries", "Subsection"],
Cell["With the symmetry rules (Remark 3.2.3) the under-crossing becomes the over-crossing, and two crossings of the same pair cancel:", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[sy[[1, 1]], withSymmetry[rulesDB]]]", "Input"],
Cell["In the graded model with q = 3 the braiding is not symmetric; with q = \:22121 and grades mod 2 (super vector spaces) it is:", "Text"],
Cell["{mG[stackL[LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}}], LD[{\"Y\", \"X\"}, {{0, tauB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}}]]] == IdentityMatrix[4], mG[stackL[LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}}], LD[{\"Y\", \"X\"}, {{0, tauB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}}]], -1, grS] == IdentityMatrix[4]}", "Input"],
Cell["56. Tests", "Section"],
Cell["Each identity is checked by the rules, in the graded model of section 53 with q = 3 (braided, not symmetric), and step by step. The symmetry identities fail for q = 3 and hold for super vector spaces.", "Text"],
Cell["all56 = Join[br, rm];\n<|\n \"Lemma 2.10 by the rules\" -> byRulesB[lem210[[1]]],\n \"Lemma 2.10: Tr(j f p) = tr_l(f)\" -> (Equal @@ hsTrace),\n \"\:00a73.1 and R2\:2013R5 by the rules (rulesDB)\" -> AllTrue[Values[all56], byRulesB],\n \"\:00a73.1 and R2\:2013R5 in the graded model (q = 3)\" -> AllTrue[Values[all56], inG],\n \"every step keeps the matrix\" -> AllTrue[Flatten[Values[all56], 1], stepsKeepG],\n \"the mirror braiding: the same identities by rules and matrices\" -> (AllTrue[Values[Map[mirror, br, {2}]], byRulesB] && AllTrue[Values[Map[mirror, br, {2}]], inG]),\n \"not symmetric for q = 3: \:03c4_Y,X \:03c4_X,Y \\[NotEqual] id, and the rules do not prove it\" -> (! inG[sy[[1]]] && ! byRulesB[sy[[1]]]),\n \"symmetric (super, q = \\[Minus]1): \:00a73.1.2 and Remark 3.2.3 by rules and matrices\" -> (AllTrue[Values[sy], byRulesB[#, withSymmetry[rulesDB]] &] && AllTrue[Values[sy], inG[#, -1, grS] &]),\n \"earlier results unchanged under rulesDB\" -> (simplifyLD[fsL, rulesDB] === fstarL && And @@ (sameQ[#[[1]], #[[2]], rulesDB] & /@ fig24) &&\n     simplifyLD[ex225a, rulesDB] === idL[{\"X*\", \"Y*\"}] && AllTrue[Values[lem22], byRules[#, rulesDB] &])\n|>", "Input"],
Cell["Appendix: what is and is not mechanised", "Section"],
Cell["Exercise 2.7.4 (sphericity is preserved by pivotal equivalences) is a statement about functors and is not mechanised.", "Item"],
Cell["Braided functors (\:00a73.1.1), Example 3.1.6 for a non-trivial 3-cocycle \:03b1, the opposite braidings of Example 3.1.8 and Exercises 3.1.9\:20133.1.11 are not mechanised; Example 3.1.6 with \:03b1 = 1, Examples 3.1.4\:20133.1.5 and the mirror (3.1.7) are the matrix models above.", "Item"],
Cell["Exercise 3.1.12 is checked for braidings (naturality for the box \:03c4_Y,Z, with (3.1) and (3.2), gives Yang\:2013Baxter); weak braidings and the rigid case are not.", "Item"],
Cell["R1 needs twists, which the book introduces in \:00a73.3; Lemma 3.1 is checked here for R2\:2013R5. The rules R4, R5 move one-line boxes through crossings; R3 is used left to right on three consecutive crossings of one kind.", "Item"],
